INT. RAILWAY LOST-PROPERTY OFFICE - NIGHT

Shelves of umbrellas, odd gloves, trombone cases. A brass bell sits on the counter. One desk lamp.

INSPECTOR WILHELMINA TOLLIVER (50s, grey tweed) enters, shakes rain off her hat, and drops it on the counter. PERCIVAL ODUYA (60s, cardigan, sleeve garters) looks up from a ledger.

She rings the bell. He flinches.

TOLLIVER
Mr. Oduya.

PERCIVAL
Inspector.

TOLLIVER
Tell me about the green suitcase.

PERCIVAL
Which green suitcase?

TOLLIVER
The one handed in on the fourteenth. Lock engraved with a swan.

PERCIVAL
Ah. That one.

TOLLIVER
You remember it, then.

PERCIVAL
I remember everything that's handed in. It's a vice.

TOLLIVER
And who handed it in?

PERCIVAL
A man in a brown coat. He said it was his sister's.

TOLLIVER
His sister's.

PERCIVAL
That's what he said.

TOLLIVER
And did you open it?

PERCIVAL
Regulations forbid it.

TOLLIVER
That isn't what I asked.

PERCIVAL
No. It isn't.

TOLLIVER
Mr. Oduya, a woman has been missing since the fourteenth. Her sister was seen at this station the same afternoon.

PERCIVAL
Perhaps the same sister.

TOLLIVER
Perhaps. Or perhaps the man in the brown coat was no brother at all.

PERCIVAL
You think I helped him.

TOLLIVER
I think you saw him.

PERCIVAL
I see everyone, Inspector. I see their umbrellas. I see their gloves. I don't see faces, only what they leave.

TOLLIVER
Then tell me what he left.

PERCIVAL
The suitcase.

TOLLIVER
Where is it?

PERCIVAL
Collected.

TOLLIVER
By whom?

PERCIVAL
By you. Yesterday. You signed the ledger.

A long silence. The lamp hums.

TOLLIVER
I did not.

PERCIVAL
Then the ledger is mistaken.

TOLLIVER
Show me.

PERCIVAL
Gladly.

He turns the ledger toward her.
